# =============================================================================
# ANAMNESIS — runtime configuration
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. The complete list; there are no other variables.
# =============================================================================

# REQUIRED. Server-side only — never serialised into a response and never
# sent to the browser. The client has no credential and never calls Gemini
# directly; every model call goes through this Node process.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# Optional. Overrides the verified default compiled into server.ts.
# Logged at startup and reported by GET /api/health, so a wrong value is
# visible before a demonstration rather than during one.
#
# Verify any value you set here actually resolves for your key:
#   curl -s "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=$GEMINI_API_KEY" | grep -o '"name": "[^"]*"'
#
# Model choice is the single biggest lever on how the demo feels. Measured
# through the analyse route on the same resized photograph:
#
#   gemini-3.7-flash    8.9s   9.6s   9.7s
#   gemini-3.6-flash   16.2s  16.5s  18.1s   (and timing out entirely under load)
#
# Capacity moves between models, so re-measure on the day rather than
# trusting these numbers. Runtime variable: changing it needs a restart,
# not a rebuild.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.7-flash

# Optional. Deadline for a single model call, in milliseconds.
#
# The API rejects anything under 10000 outright ("Minimum allowed deadline is
# 10s"), so lower values are clamped up and a warning is printed at startup.
# The effective value is reported by GET /api/health.
#
# Keep this in step with REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS in src/lib/api.ts; the browser
# must not give up before the server does. Defaults to 60000, which was
# chosen by measurement rather than assumption: a real photograph analysed
# in 17.8s on a good attempt and timed out at 32.1s three times running
# immediately before it.
GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS="60000"

# Optional. The URL where this applet is hosted. AI Studio injects it at
# runtime with the Cloud Run service URL. Nothing in the codebase reads it
# today; it is documented here because the hosting platform sets it.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# Optional. Cloud Run and most platforms inject this. Falls back to 3000.
PORT="3000"

# Optional. 'development' enables the Vite middleware; production is the
# intended default for any deployed instance.
NODE_ENV="development"

# Required in production. Both POST routes demand this as an
# x-anamnesis-key header, and refuse every request without it when
# NODE_ENV is not 'development'.
#
# Read at BUILD time too: the browser must present it, so vite compiles it
# into the client bundle (see vite.config.ts). That means anyone who opens
# devtools can read it. It is a gate against drive-by traffic on a public
# URL, not a credential — the rate limit below is what bounds the damage.
API_SHARED_SECRET="MY_SHARED_SECRET"

# Optional. Fixed-window rate limit per IP on all three POST routes.
# Defaults: 12 requests per 60000ms.
RATE_LIMIT_MAX="12"
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS="60000"

# =============================================================================
# DETECTOR A — pretrained synthetic-image classifier
#
# The manipulation verdict is produced by detectors, not by the language
# model. Detector B (signal forensics: ELA block statistics, sensor-noise
# residual, JPEG ghost) runs in the browser and needs no configuration at
# all. Detector A is the pretrained classifier and is configured here.
#
# Without HF_TOKEN the application still runs: synthetic probability reports
# NOT_ASSESSED, the manipulation confidence is still measured by Detector B,
# and the startup log says so plainly.
# =============================================================================

# Optional but strongly recommended. A Hugging Face access token with
# inference permission (https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens).
#
# Unlike API_SHARED_SECRET this is a real credential against a metered
# account, so it is server-side only and is never compiled into the bundle.
# The browser reaches the detector through POST /api/forensics/detect.
HF_TOKEN="MY_HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN"

# Optional. The classifier to use. Which detector to trust is an empirical
# question this build has NOT yet answered — the default is a starting point,
# not a validated choice. Swapping this value and re-running the benchmark
# set is the intended calibration workflow, and needs a restart rather than
# a rebuild.
#
# Candidates worth measuring against each other:
#   Organika/sdxl-detector                  (default; artificial / human)
#   umm-maybe/AI-image-detector             (artificial / human)
#   haywoodsloan/ai-image-detector-deploy   (artificial / real)
#
# Verify a model is reachable for your token before relying on it:
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}
" -X POST #     -H "Authorization: Bearer $HF_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: image/jpeg" #     --data-binary @some.jpg #     "https://api-inference.huggingface.co/models/Organika/sdxl-detector"
#
# Label vocabularies differ between models. Both sides of the question are
# matched by name (artificial/fake/synthetic vs human/real/authentic); a model
# whose labels match neither reports NOT_ASSESSED with a note rather than
# guessing which of two unknown labels means "fake".
HF_DETECTOR_MODEL="Organika/sdxl-detector"

# Optional. Hugging Face has been migrating inference to
# router.huggingface.co. Configurable so a routing change is a redeploy
# variable rather than a code change.
HF_INFERENCE_URL="https://api-inference.huggingface.co/models"

# Optional. Deadline for one detector call, in milliseconds. Clamped up to a
# 5000 floor. Defaults to 25000 — shorter than the Gemini budget, because
# this is a single forward pass and the only slow case is a cold model, which
# is worth retrying rather than waiting out.
HF_TIMEOUT_MS="25000"
